A node taken out of the middle of a ring without relinking its predecessor
leaves the ring running through an empty slot.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: link to a slot that is not a live, filled one
Report: parent's ring does not reach the slot
Report: predecessor's next is not the slot
Report: sibling ring does not close
Report: slot is not derived from its parent

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -208,9 +208,6 @@ static void detach(struct cap *n, bool adopt)
     /* n is first exactly when its predecessor links up: it is the last child then, or n itself. */
     if (pred->up) {
         node(pred->next)->child = n->up ? 0 : n->next;
-    } else {
-        pred->next = n->next;
-        pred->up = n->up;
     }
 }
 
